# Rapport d'étonnement

A fresh-eyes report captured at handover close: what surprised the corpus
operator while building the corpus — before the eyes acclimatize and the
oddities start to feel normal. This is a deliberate deliverable: the value of
a first pass over an unfamiliar codebase is the surprise, and it is lost if
not written down.

Each observation must be grounded in a corpus location (feature folder,
structural risk, known bug, reconciliation row, diagram). Do not invent;
do not turn observations into a backlog — they are knowledge, the team
decides what to do with them.

